hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27602","Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Abbas and Yunus al-Ma'na, they both said: Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Uthman ibn Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hatib, he said: My father narrated to me from his mother A'ishah bint Qudamah, she said: I was with my mother Ra'itah bint Sufyan al-Khuza'iyyah while the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was taking the pledge from the women, saying: I pledge you that you shall not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery, nor kill your children, nor bring slander that you fabricate between your hands and your feet, nor disobey in what is right. She said: So they bowed their heads, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to them: Say: Yes, as much as you are able. So they would say it, and I would say it with them, while my mother prompted me: Say, O my daughter: Yes, as much as I am able. So I would say as they said."
"27603","Haddathana Ibrahim and Yunus, they both said: Haddathana Abd al-Rahman, he said: And my father narrated to me from his mother A'ishah bint Qudamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is grievous to Allah, mighty and majestic, to take the two precious things of a Muslim and then enter him into the Fire. Yunus said: meaning his two eyes."
